 "youtube": {
  "title": "Caroline Herschel: How Did a Family Maid Find Comets?",
  "description": "Caroline Herschel was raised to be a maid, then she found eight comets. Typhus at age ten left her just four foot three, and her mother wanted her to keep house.\n\nIn England she kept house for her brother William, the astronomer. But at night she swept the sky with a small telescope, and on 1 August 1786, while William was away, she spotted a fuzzy dot that moved: her first comet. In 1787 King George III gave her a salary of 50 pounds a year: the girl raised to be a maid became the first woman paid as an astronomer.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for one strange true story a day. Had you ever heard of Caroline Herschel? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #carolineherschel #comets #stickstory",
